WEBVTT

00:00.570 --> 00:03.670
Let's say that we're told
that some angle theta, which

00:03.670 --> 00:05.300
is going to be
expressed in radians,

00:05.300 --> 00:09.580
is between negative 3 pi
over 2 and negative pi.

00:09.580 --> 00:11.235
It's greater than
negative 3 pi over 2

00:11.235 --> 00:13.840
and it's less than negative pi.

00:13.840 --> 00:18.220
And we're also told that sine
of theta is equal to 1/2.

00:18.220 --> 00:20.080
Just from this
information can we

00:20.080 --> 00:24.080
figure out what the tangent of
theta is going to be equal to?

00:24.080 --> 00:28.430
And I encourage you to pause the
video and try this on your own.

00:28.430 --> 00:30.590
In case you're stumped,
I will give you a hint.

00:30.590 --> 00:34.100
You should use the Pythagorean
identity, the fact that sine

00:34.100 --> 00:39.450
squared theta, plus cosine
squared theta is equal to 1.

00:39.450 --> 00:40.940
So let's do it.

00:40.940 --> 00:46.430
So we know the Pythagorean
identity, sine squared theta,

00:46.430 --> 00:52.830
plus cosine squared
theta is equal to 1.

00:52.830 --> 00:55.230
We know what sine
squared theta is.

00:55.230 --> 00:56.570
Sine theta is 1/2.

00:56.570 --> 01:00.250
So this could be
rewritten as 1/2 squared,

01:00.250 --> 01:06.860
plus cosine squared
theta, is equal to 1.

01:06.860 --> 01:13.450
Or we could write this as
1/4 plus cosine squared

01:13.450 --> 01:17.110
theta is equal to 1.

01:17.110 --> 01:19.890
Or we could subtract
1/4 from both sides,

01:19.890 --> 01:24.210
and we get cosine squared
theta is equal to-- let's see.

01:24.210 --> 01:25.990
You subtract 1/4 from
the left hand side,

01:25.990 --> 01:27.010
then this 1/4 goes away.

01:27.010 --> 01:28.051
That was the whole point.

01:28.051 --> 01:30.510
1 minus 1/4 is 3/4.

01:34.100 --> 01:36.870
So what could
cosine of theta be?

01:36.870 --> 01:40.280
Well, when I square
it, I get positive 3/4.

01:40.280 --> 01:44.680
So it could be the positive or
negative square root of 3/4.

01:44.680 --> 01:50.200
So cosine of theta
could be equal

01:50.200 --> 01:57.310
to the positive or negative
square root of 3 over 4,

01:57.310 --> 02:01.370
which is the same thing as
the positive or negative

02:01.370 --> 02:08.500
square root of 3, over the
square root of 4, which is 2.

02:08.500 --> 02:11.830
So it's the positive or negative
square root of 3 over 2.

02:11.830 --> 02:15.440
But how do we know which
one of these it actually is?

02:15.440 --> 02:18.200
Well, that's where this
information becomes useful.

02:22.130 --> 02:23.630
Let's draw our unit circle.

02:23.630 --> 02:24.580
If you're saying,
well, why am I even

02:24.580 --> 02:25.980
worried about cosine of theta?

02:25.980 --> 02:28.680
Well, if you know sine of
theta you know cosine of theta.

02:28.680 --> 02:31.750
Tangent of theta is just sine
of theta over cosine theta.

02:31.750 --> 02:33.760
So then you will know
the tangent of theta.

02:33.760 --> 02:35.760
But let's look at
the unit circle

02:35.760 --> 02:40.000
to figure out which value
of cosine we should use.

02:40.000 --> 02:43.890
So let me draw it,
the unit circle.

02:43.890 --> 02:45.930
That's my y-axis.

02:45.930 --> 02:49.040
That is my x-axis.

02:49.040 --> 02:52.280
And I will draw the
unit circle in pink.

02:52.280 --> 02:56.050
So that's my best attempt
at drawing a circle.

02:56.050 --> 03:00.440
Please forgive me for its
lack of perfect roundness.

03:00.440 --> 03:07.960
And it says theta is greater
than negative 3 pi over 2.

03:07.960 --> 03:09.869
So where is negative
3 pi over 2?

03:09.869 --> 03:10.410
So let's see.

03:10.410 --> 03:12.986
This is negative pi over 2.

03:12.986 --> 03:14.360
So this is one
side of the angle.

03:14.360 --> 03:15.690
Let me do this in a color.

03:15.690 --> 03:17.550
So this one side of
the angle is going

03:17.550 --> 03:18.960
to be along the positive x-axis.

03:18.960 --> 03:21.090
And we want to figure out
where the other side is.

03:21.090 --> 03:25.020
So this right over here
that's negative pi over 2.

03:25.020 --> 03:28.150
This is negative pi.

03:28.150 --> 03:31.260
So it's between negative pi,
which is right over here.

03:31.260 --> 03:32.740
So let me make that clear.

03:32.740 --> 03:36.320
Negative pi is right over here.

03:36.320 --> 03:40.860
It's between negative pi
and negative 3 pi over 2.

03:40.860 --> 03:46.430
Negative 3 pi over 2
is right over here.

03:46.430 --> 03:53.790
So our angle theta is going
to put us someplace over here.

03:57.770 --> 04:00.070
And the whole reason I did
this-- so this whole arc

04:00.070 --> 04:02.400
right here-- you
could think of this

04:02.400 --> 04:06.174
as the measure of angle
theta right over there.

04:06.174 --> 04:07.590
And the whole
reason I did that is

04:07.590 --> 04:09.340
to think about whether
the cosine of theta

04:09.340 --> 04:11.230
is going to be
positive or negative.

04:11.230 --> 04:14.120
We clearly see it's in
the second quadrant.

04:14.120 --> 04:16.079
The cosine of theta
is the x-coordinate

04:16.079 --> 04:20.160
of this point where our angle
intersects the unit circle.

04:20.160 --> 04:23.636
So this point right
over here-- actually

04:23.636 --> 04:25.010
let me do it in
that orange color

04:25.010 --> 04:29.290
again-- this right over here,
that is the cosine of theta.

04:29.290 --> 04:31.270
Now is that a positive
or negative value?

04:31.270 --> 04:33.580
Well it's clearly
a negative value.

04:33.580 --> 04:38.010
So for the sake of this
example, our cosine theta

04:38.010 --> 04:39.220
is not a positive 1.

04:39.220 --> 04:40.720
It is a negative 1
So we could write

04:40.720 --> 04:45.240
the cosine theta is equal to
the negative square root of 3

04:45.240 --> 04:46.530
over 2.

04:46.530 --> 04:48.410
So we figured out cosine
theta, but we still

04:48.410 --> 04:49.910
have to figure out
tangent of theta.

04:49.910 --> 04:51.440
And we just have
to remind ourselves

04:51.440 --> 04:53.050
that the tangent
of theta is going

04:53.050 --> 05:00.745
to be equal to the sine of
theta over the cosine of theta.

05:03.360 --> 05:05.560
Well they told us the
sine of theta is 1/2.

05:05.560 --> 05:08.520
So it's going to be 1/2
over cosine of theta, which

05:08.520 --> 05:10.260
is negative square
root of 3 over 2.

05:13.050 --> 05:14.250
And what does that equal?

05:14.250 --> 05:18.920
Well that's the same thing
as 1/2 times the reciprocal

05:18.920 --> 05:19.510
of this.

05:19.510 --> 05:27.810
So times negative 2 over
the square root of 3.

05:27.810 --> 05:31.960
These twos will cancel out and
we are left with negative 1

05:31.960 --> 05:34.160
over the square root of 3.

05:34.160 --> 05:36.850
Now some people don't like a
radical in the denominator,

05:36.850 --> 05:37.350
like this.

05:37.350 --> 05:40.120
They don't like an
irrational denominator.

05:40.120 --> 05:42.060
So we could rationalize
the denominator here

05:42.060 --> 05:44.500
by multiplying by square root
of 3 over square root of 3.

05:48.230 --> 05:52.980
And so this will be equal
to negative square root of 3

05:52.980 --> 06:04.747
over 3 is the tangent of
this angle right over here.

06:04.747 --> 06:06.830
And that actually makes
sense, because the tangent

06:06.830 --> 06:09.490
of the angle is the
slope of this line.

06:09.490 --> 06:14.199
And we see that it is
indeed a negative slope.
